]

#text(size: 0.8em)[Clark, 94 Harv. L. Rev. at 567 fig.1. Green: the professionalized half.]
]

#slide[
=== Sharing in the benefits widened as sharing in the power narrowed.

- Every shift adds division of labor and adds participation in~the~fruits~of~enterprise. #pause

- The class of capitalists widens: a wealthy elite, then public security holders, then depositors and policyholders, then benefit plan participants. #pause

- Still lopsided: about 25 million individual shareholders, but the top one percent hold over half the value. #pause

#callout["Increased sharing in benefits and decreased sharing in power: one wonders whether any of the early commentators on capitalist enterprise, from Adam Smith to Karl Marx, correctly anticipated that this would be the evolutionary pattern of the capitalist system." Clark at 568.]
]

